{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1529733-many-faced-strangers","id":1529733,"title":"Many-Faced Strangers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-30T13:21:54-08:00","id":1529733,"title":"Many-Faced Strangers","content":"So, since the companion is out, thought maybe there should be a thread for folks to discuss it. I'll start us off.<br /> <br /> So, is it worth it? I ask because I could've sworn that the pdf for the companion books came with the regular book pdf and deluxe versions. I don't remember going out of my way to select it for Dragon Blooded. I double checked, and it was included with my Sidereal and Abyssal pledges. But somehow, despite getting the Deluxe version, I guess I didn't double check to make sure I got the companion. So now I have to decide if its worth getting, because I've only been using cash and I'd have to beg a friend to get it for me.<br /> <br /> So, what kind of goodies and gems does it have? Are any of the Lunar characters stand-outs? Does the Caul scenario match up well with its Dragon-Blooded counterpart? Anything good, animal wise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T21:26:06-08:00","id":1529742,"title":"","content":"Dragon-Blooded did require you to pay for <i>Heirs to the Shogunate</i> and/or <i>The Realm</i> actually. Lunars did as well. It appears OPP changed the pricing structure after that. See also how color art and chapter fiction are just kind of assumed now instead of stretch goals.<br /> <br /> So far I'm making my way through, but the stuff on the Shadowfang Vanguard, Mount Namas, and Sublime Danger are nice additions to the shahan-ya and Lunar dominions presented. THey The first two in my view also give great texture to the Northeast and Southeast in context of the recently released <i>Across the Eight Directions</i>. I can see the Shadow Fang Vangaurd especially being on Cherak and Fray's asses, while the conflict in regards to Prasad for the Mount Namas Lunars is a nice add. And Sublime Danger seems like a really good shahan-ya for Lunars who want to do something more anti-Lookshy.<br /> <br /> The Lunar Courts, which I'm in now, also seem to add a great deal. The stuff on the disease gods gives some interesting context to the Second Contagion in At8D that I think is really cool way to show how Heavenly policy impacts how gods act.<br /> <br /> A lot of folks have commented that Ul and Aqadar are especially cool characters. And there's a range of different artifacts, but I'll have to get ot those. Also some really cool stand-out Charms, like one that lets you get Evocations from your Territory Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T08:50:50-08:00","id":1529758,"title":"","content":"I've really only looked at the one chapter in any depth so far (I'm setting up a new campaign, so my focus is largely consumed by character design/mechanics right now), but the other stuff I've glanced over has been at least interesting.<br /> <br /> I'm always happy to see new Sorcerous Initiations, so that chapter is cool, too. Granted, the Caul-based one doesn't really appeal to me, as the Caul continues to be entirely superfluous to my interests, but Witch-Pact Beast is fun. More spells, too. I don't see myself ever getting much use out of Violent Opening of Closed Portals, but it <i>is</i> amusing that the Exalted version of <i>Knock</i> involves exploding every door in your house.<br /> <br /> The additional animal-themed Martial Arts styles round out the selection a bit, so that's nice to see, too.<br /> <br /> On the subject of cool charms, I like the Heart's Blood charm that lets you get someone's form after you've sent them on a quest for personal growth/transformation. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26268,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26268-haerandir","user":"Haerandir","date":". 01-31-2024, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26268-haerandir","name":"Haerandir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-01T06:10:16-08:00","id":1529812,"title":"","content":"Witch-pact Beast sounds very interesting, as the main Lunar of my setting is a relatively stereotypical witch. As of yet, I was leaning towarda that herbology type initiation, but I've got an open mind.<br /> <br /> Likewise, I am intrigued by the necromancer Lunar, too. Sadly across Creation from my setting, thougb it could give me insight on Smiling Rat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-01T08:44:55-08:00","id":1529818,"title":"","content":"It took me a bit to understand Thousand Blades Style. It sounds like the martial artist has to pick a single type of artifact weapon as their &quot;signature weapon&quot; (preferably a type of which they can obtain multiple examples), but how narrowly is the signature weapon defined? If the martial artist chooses daiklaves as their signature weapon (let's assume the daiklave they originally trained with was a &quot;normal&quot; straight-sword daiklave), can they add a reaper daiklave to their Arsenal?<br /> <br /> ...Perhaps more importantly, is there any way to learn another signature weapon? It seems weirdly limiting that a style which encourages owning multiple artifact weapons would require them all to be the same type.<br /> <br /> (Honestly, the first couple times I read the paragraph about signature weapons, I thought the martial artist had to pick <i>one specific weapon</i> and was really confused as to <i>how</i> you were supposed to get more signature weapons to increase your Arsenal.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-01T09:43:21-08:00","id":1529820,"title":"","content":"I had wondered about that, too. I think that my house rule on that would be that if weapons are considered different enough to have separate entries in the weapon list, then they're different enough to not share signature weapon status. The only exception I can think of might be regular and reaper daiklaves, as they are mechanically identical. So, maybe the deciding factor should be weapon size category + tags.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, I don't expect it to come up in my campaign, as the martial artist PC is also a sorcerer who uses Wood Dragon's Claw as their primary weapon, so they're unlikely to branch out into daiklaves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26268-haerandir","name":"Haerandir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-01T23:26:35-08:00","id":1529848,"title":"","content":"I think it's worth it, but I'm biased because my wife's character gets a page fiction and accompanying art in it. =3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T16:04:04-08:00","id":1531555,"title":"","content":"I've only started skimming it, but for the moment I like most of what I've read. I'm a bit disappointed that the Martial Arts are not more Lunar focused, and there are still minor mistakes, like forgetting the Cheetah's speed bonus, but some of the Charms are really good, the Artifacts and their backstories are nice, the animals avatars are a cool concept and I might use a Great Leech as a spirit shape for a future character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T21:26:00-08:00","id":1531583,"title":"","content":"Hm. Can Thousand Blades Style Charms be used together with other Martial Arts styles that are compatible with the stylist's chosen signature weapon? Or does it not really make sense to blend telekinetic weapon control with combat techniques that involve actual, like, stances?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T23:15:39-08:00","id":1531595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1529733-many-faced-strangers?p=1531583#post1531583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. Can Thousand Blades Style Charms be used together with other Martial Arts styles that are compatible with the stylist's chosen signature weapon? Or does it not really make sense to blend telekinetic weapon control with combat techniques that involve actual, like, stances?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is nothing that says it isn't compatible, so it is compatible per normal MA rules.<br /> I'd also argue that the stylist can simply position the weapons where they would be if she were in the stance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T02:09:38-08:00","id":1531838,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to say thank you to whoever wrote World-Soul Awakening. That Charm is amazing.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm wondering: Can Thousand Blades Style Charms be used in animal shape?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":1405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","user":"Anteros","date":". 03-02-2024, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T06:11:32-08:00","id":1531952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1529733-many-faced-strangers?p=1531838#post1531838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'm wondering: Can Thousand Blades Style Charms be used in animal shape?</div> </div> </div> </div>I should think so. It even specifically calls out that the style has no basis in 'traditional martial techniques', meaning that there's no requirement that you be able to move in a particular manner.<br /> <br /> Now that you mention it, I suspect that this is the reason the style was included in the Lunars companion book in the first place.<br /> <br /> Exalted's answer to sharks with frickin' lasers on their heads is &quot;sharks wielding frickin' direlances with telekinesis,&quot; I guess.<br /> <br /> Note: I am far from an expert on Lunars, and I wrote this at work, so maybe favor vwllss trnt prncss' answer below over mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26268,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26268-haerandir","user":"Haerandir","date":".  Added note. 03-05-2024, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26268-haerandir","name":"Haerandir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T19:52:05-08:00","id":1531990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1529733-many-faced-strangers?p=1531838#post1531838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'm wondering: Can Thousand Blades Style Charms be used in animal shape?</div> </div> </div> </div>It cannot, no martial arts can. Lunars have to choose between MA fighting and animal-form fighting.<br /> I'd not recommend houseruling it without extensively checking on what the interactions would be. Even if you preclude offensive merits from compatibility, having animal form defensive merits (soak, Tiny, etc) could easily get overbearing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T19:09:14-08:00","id":1532070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haerandir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1529733-many-faced-strangers?p=1531952#post1531952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I should think so. It even specifically calls out that the style has no basis in 'traditional martial techniques', meaning that there's no requirement that you be able to move in a particular manner.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a reasonable point that somebody could make in favour of it, but I wouldn't personally go along with it because I feel as though even if you have a Martial Art that isn't rooted in mundane fighting style, the term and the associations carry with them a certain vibe that I think matches best with a humanoid form (for those few martial artists where the distinction matters in the first place).<br /> <br /> ...The very small number of martial arts powers that entail their own brand of shapeshifting notwithstanding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haerandir</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that you mention it, I suspect that this is the reason the style was included in the Lunars companion book in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I think that speaks to one thing where part of the intention with Lunars in this Edition has been to emphasize imagery for them as heroes that is more expansive than the animal forms. Something that came up pretty early in the days when a new Edition was announced was the intention to make a Lunar sword fighter feel like a viable character in a mechanical sense, and I think that sentiment worked its way through to the current signature Full Moon. Tegama Asarkon is modelled as a sword fighter first, to the point that he's said to almost always fight in human form, while he still has legitimacy as a Lunar (particularly exemplified in the chapter fiction of how he lured a Dynast into a trap).<br /> <br /> I would say that was why Sublime Danger was first designed as somebody using a unique new martial art that gave her the iconic feature of wings made of daiklaves, more than an idea that it would be a style well suited to somebody who might turn into an animal. And so it ends up in the book because so did she, and you couldn't really have one without the other.<br /> <br /> On top of which, I think there's something to giving Lunars a few achievements or inventions that aren't a function of their shapeshifting and animalistic side.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T11:37:18-08:00","id":1532246,"title":"","content":"I get the reasoning, but it's kind of sad that none of the martial arts in the Lunar Companion book is particularly convenient for Lunar use.<br /> <br /> I had another question, about the Witch-Beast Pact this time. Can a magical creature that would usually be a 2-dots familiar be enhanced somehow to fit as a familiar for this Sorcerous initiation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T06:40:13-07:00","id":1532371,"title":"","content":"It appears that the only real restriction is that you can't have your Witch-Beast familiar be a creature that would be a 3-dot familiar without magic. I think the reasoning is that some 3-dot familiars are expensive because they're uniquely useful, and some 3-dot familiars are expensive because they're uniquely dangerous, and the devs don't want you double-dipping by getting what amounts to a combat retainer, plus sorcery, for the same low price. Having an already-magical familiar be what amounts to a special effect for other Charms/Merits you've purchased doesn't seem to ring the same alarm bells.<br /> <br /> One of the examples given for a 3-dot magical familiar in the core book is a fire-breathing ox, so it's clearly not size-linked, and doesn't preclude having <i>some</i> combat utility. So if, say, you want a talking horse that can teach you magic, I would allow that as a Storyteller. I can see how some Storytellers wouldn't feel comfortable with that, but there's always an element of judgement and personal world-building between chronicles. Honestly I find the whole 'no apex predators' to be a bit of an unnecessary restriction, myself. As I mention above, it doesn't actually change anything about your character mechanically (versus having a 3-dot combat Familiar and a different Sorcerous Initiation), so it's pretty much a flavor limitation (i.e. you can be a Fighty Beastmaster or a Mystic Beastmaster, but not both).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26268-haerandir","name":"Haerandir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T16:49:11-07:00","id":1532739,"title":"","content":"Ok, so I could take say, a Giant Grosbeak or a Silere (from Hundred Devils Night Parade), that would only be a 2 dots familiar, without needing to beef them up somehow, then.<br /> <br /> Oh, and other question: would the -3 penalty on attacks rolls while using the Wings mutations apply to withering attacks with Laughing Hyena Mockery?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T07:35:27-07:00","id":1537340,"title":"","content":"Hundred Devils Night Parade states that the great roc would be available in Chapter 5 of Many-Faced Strangers, but this doesn't seem to be the case. Does anyone know if this an oversight or a change of plans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28503-htuein","name":"Htuein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T13:05:14-07:00","id":1537521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Htuein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1529733-many-faced-strangers?p=1537340#post1537340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hundred Devils Night Parade states that the great roc would be available in Chapter 5 of Many-Faced Strangers</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't seem to find that. Would you have a page reference?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T05:50:06-07:00","id":1537555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1529733-many-faced-strangers?p=1537521#post1537521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't seem to find that. Would you have a page reference?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s on page 185 under the mospid stat block.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28503-htuein","name":"Htuein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T06:19:08-07:00","id":1537556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Htuein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1529733-many-faced-strangers?p=1537555#post1537555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s on page 185 under the mospid stat block.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. That is honestly not in my copy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T06:30:13-07:00","id":1537558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1529733-many-faced-strangers?p=1537556#post1537556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. That is honestly not in my copy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just redownloaded it from DriveThruRPG to check if it was edited out in an update at some point, and it is still there. Maybe it\u2019s only in the digital copies if you have a physical copy. The whole thing seems pretty strange though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28503-htuein","name":"Htuein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T06:56:24-07:00","id":1537559,"title":"","content":"It's in the copy that I have.<br /> <br /> It's a little red blurb on page 185 and says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> GREAT ROCS<br /> The great roc is a larger cousin to the Metagalapan riding hawk, and can be found in Chapter 5 of Many-Faced Strangers. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T12:48:17-07:00","id":1537575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1529733-many-faced-strangers?p=1529812#post1529812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Witch-pact Beast sounds very interesting, as the main Lunar of my setting is a relatively stereotypical witch. As of yet, I was leaning towarda that herbology type initiation, but I've got an open mind.<br /> <br /> Likewise, I am intrigued by the necromancer Lunar, too. Sadly across Creation from my setting, thougb it could give me insight on Smiling Rat.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the beauty of how 3e Lunars seem to work - the network of favors &amp; mentoring allows for the possibility of Lunars from anywhere, even opposite sides of Creation, to be connected somehow through &quot;i know someone who knows someone&quot;, exchange of pupils, information and so on.<br /> <br /> Smiling Rat being a past teacher, brother-in-arms, pupil, ally, rival or more from a lunar warlord, recluse sorcerer, wandering warrior-exorcist or anything else that catches your fancy to insert in your setting is <i><b>completely</b></i> possible and fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-03T10:58:42-08:00","id":1548910,"title":"","content":"So, the special activation rules for Thousand Blades Form let you apply the attunement discount to Glorious Solar Saber and similar Charms. Can GSS be activated multiple times in this way -- e.g., attuning one daiklave and then activating GSS four times (for one mote each) to max out your Arsenal rating?<br /> <br /> (Honestly, I still find it kind of bizarre that you have to pick one kind of artifact weapon for the style and can't have a mix of (artifact) swords and spears and axes flying around.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-04T03:13:23-08:00","id":1548940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1529733-many-faced-strangers?p=1548910#post1548910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Honestly, I still find it kind of bizarre that you have to pick one kind of artifact weapon for the style and can't have a mix of (artifact) swords and spears and axes flying around.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I dislike that aspect because I think it helps push player characters with the style towards maximising their Arsenal rating during character creation and then viewing their weapons purely in terms of quantity. I'd much prefer if the style encouraged taking trophies from defeated enemies, who, naturally, don\u2019t always favour the same artifact weapons as the PC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}